Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:11:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Do not re-register the spdlog logger
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the last client has quit from hailort_service, the logger is
not torn down because there is no destructor in HailoRTOSLogger.

The next client crashes hailort_service, because the already
existing logger cannot be re-registered via the current code.

To minimize the changes, query whether a logger with the expected
name already exists in the HailoRTOSLogger constructor and use that.

Signed-off-by: Zoltán Böszörményi <zboszor@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/hailo-ai/hailort/pull/51]
---
 hailort/common/os/posix/os_utils.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hailort/common/os/posix/os_utils.cpp b/hailort/common/os/posix/os_utils.cpp
index 3bfca66..e61501d 100644
--- a/hailort/common/os/posix/os_utils.cpp
+++ b/hailort/common/os/posix/os_utils.cpp
@@ -27,7 +27,12 @@ namespace hailort
 
 HailoRTOSLogger::HailoRTOSLogger()
 {
-    m_hailort_os_logger = spdlog::syslog_logger_mt("syslog", "hailort_service", LOG_PID);
+    std::shared_ptr<spdlog::logger> logger = spdlog::get("hailort_service");
+
+    if (logger != nullptr)
+        m_hailort_os_logger = logger;
+    else
+        m_hailort_os_logger = spdlog::syslog_logger_mt("syslog", "hailort_service", LOG_PID);
     m_hailort_os_logger->set_pattern("%v");
     m_hailort_os_logger->set_level(spdlog::level::debug);
 }
